WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.767
Write and send an email campaign.

00:00:03.433 --> 00:00:06.433
Campaigns. Campaigns are written here.

00:00:06.933 --> 00:00:17.667
Start from a season. Each card brings the wording, a button and who should get it. New campaign starts blank; Open finishes a draft. The tour opens this one.

00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:23.800
The email. What the customer reads. The preview on the right changes as you type.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:30.467
Campaign name. Only the office sees it, e.g. Spring cleanup 2027.

00:00:30.967 --> 00:00:37.267
Subject line. What they see in their inbox. {first_name} becomes each customer's first name.

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:46.967
The message. Your own wording. A blank line starts a new paragraph; {first_name}, {company} and {company_phone} are filled in for each customer.

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:55.633
The button. The big button in the email, e.g. Book a spring cleanup, and its link: your request form once it is set up.

00:00:56.133 --> 00:01:01.567
Design. How it looks in the inbox: layout, colour, pictures and headline.

00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:11.300
Layout. Photo header puts a wide photo of your work on top; Colour banner a coloured band with the headline; Plain is a simple letter.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:20.467
Header picture. Paste a picture link or press Upload. A wide landscape photo, at least 1200 px across, looks best.

00:01:20.967 --> 00:01:25.033
Colour banner. The tour puts the starter's colour banner back.

00:01:25.533 --> 00:01:34.067
Colour. Six brand colours for the banner and the button: bay navy, paver red, lawn green, sand gold, slate and violet.

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:41.367
Headline. The big words at the top, and a line under them (e.g. Reserve your spot before April).

00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:50.133
A picture in the message. An optional photo in the body, from a link or Upload. Once it's added, a Caption box appears.

00:01:50.633 --> 00:01:55.900
Who gets it. Choose the customers. The count at the bottom updates as you go.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:01.967
Customers or leads. Customers, Leads, Both, or Inactive customers.

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:07.233
Residential or commercial. Any, Residential or Commercial.

00:02:07.733 --> 00:02:15.900
Towns. Click towns to send only there; none picked means everywhere. The number is how many customers each town has.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:27.033
Narrow it down. Had a kind of work in the last N months, lost an estimate lately, no work lately, on a maintenance plan or not. Demo customers stay out.

00:02:27.533 --> 00:02:36.267
How many get it. The count, a few names and a bar by town. Customers who opted out, or have no email, are never included.

00:02:36.767 --> 00:02:44.633
Send a test first. Type your email and press Send test to see it in a real inbox. It saves the draft first.

00:02:45.133 --> 00:02:50.800
Save draft. Keeps the campaign as a draft to finish later. The tour doesn't save.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:03:00.667
Send it. Sends to everyone counted, paced per hour (it asks first, and you can Stop it while it goes out). Greyed out until live email is on.

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:07.767
What they'll see. A live preview with a sample customer's name, updated as you type and design.

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:14.367
Back to campaigns. Leaves the composer. Nothing is kept unless you pressed Save draft.

00:03:14.867 --> 00:03:20.467
That's it. You can play this tour in the app any time: press Help, and ask in your own words.
